    <span class=3D"nf">call</span>    <span class=3D"nv">___chkstk_ms</span=
>
    <span class=3D"nf">subq</span>    <span class=3D"o">%</span><span class=
=3D"nb">rax</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"o">%</span><spa=
n class=3D"nb">rsp</span>
    <span class=3D"nf">leaq</span>    <span class=3D"mi">32</span><span cla=
ss=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"o">%</span><span class=3D"nb">rsp</span><sp=
an class=3D"p">),</span> <span class=3D"o">%</span><span class=3D"nb">rcx</=
span>
    <span class=3D"nf">call</span>    <span class=3D"nv">callee</span>
    <span class=3D"nf">addq</span>    <span class=3D"kc">$</span><span clas=
s=3D"mi">1048616</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"o">%</span=
><span class=3D"nb">rsp</span>
    <span class=3D"nf">ret</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>I used GCC, but this is practically identical to the code generated by
MSVC and Clang. Note the call to <code class=3D"language-plaintext highligh=
ter-rouge">___chkstk_ms</code> in the function prologue
before allocating the stack frame (<code class=3D"language-plaintext highli=
ghter-rouge">subq</code>). Also note that it sets <code class=3D"language-p=
laintext highlighter-rouge">eax</code>.
As a volatile register, this would normally accomplish nothing because
it=E2=80=99s done just before a function call, but recall that <code class=
=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">___chkstk_ms</code> has
a custom ABI. That=E2=80=99s the argument to chkstk. Further note that it u=
ses
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">rax</code> on the retu=
rn. That=E2=80=99s not the value returned by chkstk, but rather
that x64 <em>chkstk preserves all registers</em>.</p>

<p>Well, maybe. The official documentation says that registers <a href=3D"h=
ttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/prolog-and-epilog">r10 and r11
are volatile</a>, but that information conflicts with Microsoft=E2=80=99s o=
wn
implementation. Just in case, I choose a conservative interpretation that
all registers are preserved.</p>

<h3 id=3D"implementing-chkstk">Implementing chkstk</h3>

<p>In a high level language, chkstk might look something like so:</p>

<div class=3D"language-c highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre c=
lass=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c1">// NOTE: hypothetical implement=
ation</span>
<span class=3D"kt">void</span> <span class=3D"nf">___chkstk_ms</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"kt">ptrdiff_t</span> <span class=3D"n">f=
rame_size</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"p">{</span>
    <span class=3D"k">volatile</span> <span class=3D"kt">char</span> <span =
class=3D"n">frame</span><span class=3D"p">[</span><span class=3D"n">frame_s=
ize</span><span class=3D"p">];</span>  <span class=3D"c1">// NOTE: variable=
-length array</span>
    <span class=3D"k">for</span> <span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"k=
t">ptrdiff_t</span> <span class=3D"n">i</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span>=
